            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding the discharge of your 89-year-old male patient, admitted on 10/10/2014 with symptomatic aortic valve regurgitation. On admission, clinical examination revealed signs of volume overload with peripheral oedema and mild dyspnoea. Electrocardiography showed sinus rhythm without acute ischaemic changes. Chest X-ray demonstrated cardiomegaly. Echocardiography confirmed severe aortic regurgitation with preserved left ventricular systolic function and significant annular dilatation. Blood tests revealed mildly elevated BNP with otherwise stable renal and hepatic parameters. Given the patient's advanced age and considerable operative risk, the multidisciplinary team decided against surgical intervention. Medical management was optimised with vasodilator therapy and diuretics. The patient responded well, with symptomatic improvement. Discharge medications and outpatient cardiology follow-up have been arranged. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
